{"name":"Orange Chiffon","hex":"#f9ae7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"chiffon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns made of silk, polyester, or cotton.","Any purely ornamental accessory on a woman's dress, such as a bunch of ribbon, lace, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chiffon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chiffon (fabric)","blocks":[{"text":"Chiffon, from the French word chiffe which means \"cloth or rag\"; is a lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns. Crepe yarn tends to have a tighter twist than standard yarns. The twist in the crepe yarns puckers the fabric slightly in both directions after weaving, giving it some stretch and a slightly rough feel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Lillian_Gish_2.jpg/330px-Lillian_Gish_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiffon_(fabric)","wikidata":"Q691189"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour 